kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[3]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  modify_requirement,tui21,"widget-usage-policy","The TUI MUST NOT be constrained to hand-rolled cell loops: ratatui-widgets (the independent crate, NOT the umbrella ratatui) is an allowed dependency, and its subset (Paragraph/Block/List/ListState/Clear) MAY be reused when it fits. When a library widget does not meet the inline-rendering need (e.g. a specific CJK/emoji behavior, or a custom interaction), the TUI MAY instead build a self-contained widget on top of ratatui-core primitives (Buffer/Layout/Style/Text/Widget trait). The umbrella ratatui crate MUST remain absent (see tui20). The choice between reuse and self-build MUST be driven by fit, not by a blanket prohibition.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui41,"render-test-coverage","The TUI rendering layer MUST be covered by TestBackend-based tests (ratatui_core::backend::TestBackend) that assert buffer content via assert_buffer_lines, covering at minimum: the draw_tail_frame path (empty and streaming states), the commit_to_scrollback insert_before path (including CJK double-width line commit), streaming text wrapping at terminal width, and TurnEnd tail flush. This replaces implementation-bound hand-written unit tests with behavior-level render assertions. Evidence: codex uses TestBackend + insta snapshots (codex-rs/tui snapshots/, docs/tui-research/codex.md §3); ratatui official tests use TestBackend + Viewport::Inline + insert_before (ratatui/tests/terminal.rs:66); the prior commit_to_scrollback cell loop (terminal.rs:86-119) had zero test coverage.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui42,"render-business-decoupling","The TUI rendering layer MUST be decoupled from the agent data/business flow: rendering functions MUST consume UI-only data types (e.g. a RenderedLine enum: UserInput/AssistantText/ToolSummary/Status) rather than domain XyEvent variants directly. The boundary between the UI/UX layer and the data-flow/business-flow layer MUST be explicit: business events (XyEvent) are translated into UI data types at a single seam, and the rendering layer MUST NOT match on XyEvent variants or call Driver/agent methods. Evidence: the current render::commit_lines_for (src/app/tui/render.rs:119) and app::handle_xy_event (src/app/tui/app.rs:102) mix XyEvent handling with line production, coupling rendering to the domain event vocabulary; codex isolates via HistoryCell (codex-rs/tui/src/history_cell/) and pi via typed message parts (packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/assistant-message.ts).",null,null,null
op_scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui21,"widget-choice-driven-by-fit","a TUI rendering path needs to display wrapped text or a bordered box","the implementation is chosen","either a ratatui-widgets subset (Paragraph/Block) is reused OR a self-contained widget is built on ratatui-core primitives and neither choice is blocked by a blanket prohibition"
  tui21,"umbrella-still-absent","Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are inspected after the change","dependency names are checked","the umbrella ratatui crate is absent while ratatui-core and ratatui-crossterm remain (and ratatui-widgets may be present)"
  tui41,"render-harness-covers-commit","commit_to_scrollback renders a CJK line via insert_before","the TestBackend buffer is asserted","the double-width characters occupy two columns and the assertion uses assert_buffer_lines not per-cell hand-rolled checks"
  tui42,"no-xyevent-in-render","the TUI rendering functions are inspected","their input types are checked","they consume UI-only data types (e.g. RenderedLine) and no rendering function matches on XyEvent variants or calls Driver/agent methods"
